#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "gitrepository-layout(5)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:7
msgid "gitrepository-layout - Git Repository Layout"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:11
msgid "$GIT_DIR/*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:13
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:16
msgid "A Git repository comes in two different flavours:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:18
msgid "a `.git` directory at the root of the working tree;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:23
msgid ""
"a `<project>.git` directory that is a 'bare' repository (i.e. without its "
"own working tree), that is typically used for exchanging histories with "
"others by pushing into it and fetching from it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Note*: Also you can have a plain text file `.git` at the root of\n"
"your working tree, containing `gitdir: <path>` to point at the real\n"
"directory that has the repository.\n"
"This mechanism is called a 'gitfile' and is usually managed via the\n"
"`git submodule` and `git worktree` commands. It is often used for\n"
"a working tree of a submodule checkout, to allow you in the\n"
"containing superproject to `git checkout` a branch that does not\n"
"have the submodule.  The `checkout` has to remove the entire\n"
"submodule working tree, without losing the submodule repository.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:35
msgid "These things may exist in a Git repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "objects"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:41
msgid ""
"Object store associated with this repository.  Usually an object store is "
"self sufficient (i.e. all the objects that are referred to by an object "
"found in it are also found in it), but there are a few ways to violate it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:44
msgid ""
"You could have an incomplete but locally usable repository by creating a "
"shallow clone.  See linkgit:git-clone[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:51
msgid ""
"You could be using the `objects/info/alternates` or "
"`$GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES` mechanisms to 'borrow' objects from "
"other object stores.  A repository with this kind of incomplete object store "
"is not suitable to be published for use with dumb transports but otherwise "
"is OK as long as `objects/info/alternates` points at the object stores it "
"borrows from."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:54
msgid ""
"This directory is ignored if $GIT_COMMON_DIR is set and "
"\"$GIT_COMMON_DIR/objects\" will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "objects/[0-9a-f][0-9a-f]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:62
msgid ""
"A newly created object is stored in its own file.  The objects are splayed "
"over 256 subdirectories using the first two characters of the sha1 object "
"name to keep the number of directory entries in `objects` itself to a "
"manageable number. Objects found here are often called 'unpacked' (or "
"'loose') objects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:63
#, no-wrap
msgid "objects/pack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:67
msgid ""
"Packs (files that store many objects in compressed form, along with index "
"files to allow them to be randomly accessed) are found in this directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "objects/info"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:71
msgid "Additional information about the object store is recorded in this directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "objects/info/packs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:79
msgid ""
"This file is to help dumb transports discover what packs are available in "
"this object store.  Whenever a pack is added or removed, `git "
"update-server-info` should be run to keep this file up to date if the "
"repository is published for dumb transports.  'git repack' does this by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "objects/info/alternates"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:90
msgid ""
"This file records paths to alternate object stores that this object store "
"borrows objects from, one pathname per line. Note that not only native Git "
"tools use it locally, but the HTTP fetcher also tries to use it remotely; "
"this will usually work if you have relative paths (relative to the object "
"database, not to the repository!) in your alternates file, but it will not "
"work if you use absolute paths unless the absolute path in filesystem and "
"web URL is the same. See also `objects/info/http-alternates`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:91
#, no-wrap
msgid "objects/info/http-alternates"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:95
msgid ""
"This file records URLs to alternate object stores that this object store "
"borrows objects from, to be used when the repository is fetched over HTTP."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "refs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:104
msgid ""
"References are stored in subdirectories of this directory.  The 'git prune' "
"command knows to preserve objects reachable from refs found in this "
"directory and its subdirectories.  This directory is ignored (except "
"refs/bisect, refs/rewritten and refs/worktree) if $GIT_COMMON_DIR is set and "
"\"$GIT_COMMON_DIR/refs\" will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:105
#, no-wrap
msgid "refs/heads/`name`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:107
msgid "records tip-of-the-tree commit objects of branch `name`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:108
#, no-wrap
msgid "refs/tags/`name`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:111
msgid ""
"records any object name (not necessarily a commit object, or a tag object "
"that points at a commit object)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:112
#, no-wrap
msgid "refs/remotes/`name`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:115
msgid ""
"records tip-of-the-tree commit objects of branches copied from a remote "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "refs/replace/`<obj-sha1>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:121
msgid ""
"records the SHA-1 of the object that replaces `<obj-sha1>`.  This is similar "
"to info/grafts and is internally used and maintained by "
"linkgit:git-replace[1]. Such refs can be exchanged between repositories "
"while grafts are not."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "packed-refs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:127
msgid ""
"records the same information as refs/heads/, refs/tags/, and friends record "
"in a more efficient way.  See linkgit:git-pack-refs[1]. This file is ignored "
"if $GIT_COMMON_DIR is set and \"$GIT_COMMON_DIR/packed-refs\" will be used "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:128
#, no-wrap
msgid "HEAD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:139
msgid ""
"A symref (see glossary) to the `refs/heads/` namespace describing the "
"currently active branch.  It does not mean much if the repository is not "
"associated with any working tree (i.e. a 'bare' repository), but a valid Git "
"repository *must* have the HEAD file; some porcelains may use it to guess "
"the designated \"default\" branch of the repository (usually 'master').  It "
"is legal if the named branch 'name' does not (yet) exist.  In some legacy "
"setups, it is a symbolic link instead of a symref that points at the current "
"branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:144
msgid ""
"HEAD can also record a specific commit directly, instead of being a symref "
"to point at the current branch.  Such a state is often called 'detached "
"HEAD.' See linkgit:git-checkout[1] for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:145
#, no-wrap
msgid "config"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:149
msgid ""
"Repository specific configuration file. This file is ignored if "
"$GIT_COMMON_DIR is set and \"$GIT_COMMON_DIR/config\" will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "config.worktree"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:154
msgid ""
"Working directory specific configuration file for the main working directory "
"in multiple working directory setup (see linkgit:git-worktree[1])."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:156
#, no-wrap
msgid "branches"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:166
msgid ""
"A deprecated way to store shorthands to be used to specify a URL to 'git "
"fetch', 'git pull' and 'git push'.  A file can be stored as "
"`branches/<name>` and then 'name' can be given to these commands in place of "
"'repository' argument.  See the REMOTES section in linkgit:git-fetch[1] for "
"details.  This mechanism is legacy and not likely to be found in modern "
"repositories. This directory is ignored if $GIT_COMMON_DIR is set and "
"\"$GIT_COMMON_DIR/branches\" will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:168
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:247
msgid "Git will stop reading remotes from this directory in Git 3.0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "hooks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:179
msgid ""
"Hooks are customization scripts used by various Git commands.  A handful of "
"sample hooks are installed when 'git init' is run, but all of them are "
"disabled by default.  To enable, the `.sample` suffix has to be removed from "
"the filename by renaming.  Read linkgit:githooks[5] for more details about "
"each hook. This directory is ignored if $GIT_COMMON_DIR is set and "
"\"$GIT_COMMON_DIR/hooks\" will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:180
#, no-wrap
msgid "common"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:185
msgid ""
"When multiple working trees are used, most of files in $GIT_DIR are "
"per-worktree with a few known exceptions. All files under 'common' however "
"will be shared between all working trees."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:186
#, no-wrap
msgid "index"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:189
msgid ""
"The current index file for the repository.  It is usually not found in a "
"bare repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:190
#, no-wrap
msgid "sharedindex.<SHA-1>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:193
msgid ""
"The shared index part, to be referenced by $GIT_DIR/index and other "
"temporary index files. Only valid in split index mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:194
#, no-wrap
msgid "info"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:198
msgid ""
"Additional information about the repository is recorded in this "
"directory. This directory is ignored if $GIT_COMMON_DIR is set and "
"\"$GIT_COMMON_DIR/info\" will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:199
#, no-wrap
msgid "info/refs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:208
msgid ""
"This file helps dumb transports discover what refs are available in this "
"repository.  If the repository is published for dumb transports, this file "
"should be regenerated by 'git update-server-info' every time a tag or branch "
"is created or modified.  This is normally done from the `hooks/update` hook, "
"which is run by the 'git-receive-pack' command when you 'git push' into the "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:209
#, no-wrap
msgid "info/grafts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:216
msgid ""
"This file records fake commit ancestry information, to pretend the set of "
"parents a commit has is different from how the commit was actually created.  "
"One record per line describes a commit and its fake parents by listing their "
"40-byte hexadecimal object names separated by a space and terminated by a "
"newline."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:220
msgid ""
"Note that the grafts mechanism is outdated and can lead to problems "
"transferring objects between repositories; see linkgit:git-replace[1] for a "
"more flexible and robust system to do the same thing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:221
#, no-wrap
msgid "info/exclude"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:227
msgid ""
"This file, by convention among Porcelains, stores the exclude pattern "
"list. `.gitignore` is the per-directory ignore file.  'git status', 'git "
"add', 'git rm' and 'git clean' look at it but the core Git commands do not "
"look at it.  See also: linkgit:gitignore[5]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:228
#, no-wrap
msgid "info/attributes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:231
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Defines which attributes to assign to a path, similar to per-directory\n"
"`.gitattributes` files.   See also: linkgit:gitattributes[5].\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:232
#, no-wrap
msgid "info/sparse-checkout"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:235
msgid ""
"This file stores sparse checkout patterns.  See also: "
"linkgit:git-read-tree[1]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "remotes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:245
msgid ""
"Stores shorthands for URL and default refnames for use when interacting with "
"remote repositories via 'git fetch', 'git pull' and 'git push' commands.  "
"See the REMOTES section in linkgit:git-fetch[1] for details.  This mechanism "
"is legacy and not likely to be found in modern repositories. This directory "
"is ignored if $GIT_COMMON_DIR is set and \"$GIT_COMMON_DIR/remotes\" will be "
"used instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:249
#, no-wrap
msgid "logs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:254
msgid ""
"Records of changes made to refs are stored in this directory.  See "
"linkgit:git-update-ref[1] for more information. This directory is ignored "
"(except logs/HEAD) if $GIT_COMMON_DIR is set and \"$GIT_COMMON_DIR/logs\" "
"will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:255
#, no-wrap
msgid "logs/refs/heads/`name`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:257
msgid "Records all changes made to the branch tip named `name`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:258
#, no-wrap
msgid "logs/refs/tags/`name`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:260
msgid "Records all changes made to the tag named `name`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:261
#, no-wrap
msgid "shallow"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:267
msgid ""
"This is similar to `info/grafts` but is internally used and maintained by "
"shallow clone mechanism.  See `--depth` option to linkgit:git-clone[1] and "
"linkgit:git-fetch[1]. This file is ignored if $GIT_COMMON_DIR is set and "
"\"$GIT_COMMON_DIR/shallow\" will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:268
#, no-wrap
msgid "commondir"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:274
msgid ""
"If this file exists, $GIT_COMMON_DIR (see linkgit:git[1]) will be set to the "
"path specified in this file if it is not explicitly set. If the specified "
"path is relative, it is relative to $GIT_DIR. The repository with commondir "
"is incomplete without the repository pointed by \"commondir\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:275
#, no-wrap
msgid "modules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:277
msgid "Contains the git-repositories of the submodules."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:278
#, no-wrap
msgid "worktrees"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:284
msgid ""
"Contains administrative data for linked working trees. Each subdirectory "
"contains the working tree-related part of a linked working tree. This "
"directory is ignored if $GIT_COMMON_DIR is set, in which case "
"\"$GIT_COMMON_DIR/worktrees\" will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:285
#, no-wrap
msgid "worktrees/<id>/gitdir"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:291
msgid ""
"A text file containing the absolute path back to the .git file that points "
"to here. This is used to check if the linked repository has been manually "
"removed and there is no need to keep this directory any more. The mtime of "
"this file should be updated every time the linked repository is accessed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:292
#, no-wrap
msgid "worktrees/<id>/locked"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:298
msgid ""
"If this file exists, the linked working tree may be on a portable device and "
"not available. The presence of this file prevents `worktrees/<id>` from "
"being pruned either automatically or manually by `git worktree prune`. The "
"file may contain a string explaining why the repository is locked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:299
#, no-wrap
msgid "worktrees/<id>/config.worktree"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:301
msgid "Working directory specific configuration file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:305
#, no-wrap
msgid "SEE ALSO"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:315
msgid ""
"linkgit:git-init[1], linkgit:git-clone[1], linkgit:git-config[1], "
"linkgit:git-fetch[1], linkgit:git-pack-refs[1], linkgit:git-gc[1], "
"linkgit:git-checkout[1], linkgit:gitglossary[7], link:user-manual.html[The "
"Git User's Manual]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:317
#, no-wrap
msgid "GIT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitrepository-layout.adoc:318
msgid "Part of the linkgit:git[1] suite"
msgstr ""
